KG42.register("source_edge_archive-1590b241ad3d8cf8157ebcba",{"id":"01-central_pool::v141-c-R004::E::v141-c-R004-E001","paper":"01-central_pool","rule_id":"v141-c-R004","rule_ref":"01-central_pool::v141-c-R004","record":{"edge_id":"v141-c-R004-E001","source":"clearing.local","target":"execution.energy_trade","type":"links","constraint_ids":["v141-c-R004-C001"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-e011"]},"evidence_class":"S","provenance_gate":"direct_C_edge_with_constraint_and_source_excerpt","scientific_acceptance":false,"accepted_constraint_ids":["v141-c-R004-C001"],"held_constraint_ids":[],"semantic_review_status":"supported","source":"COMP-f0015e75a5829a38","target":"COMP-f0015e75a5829a38","source_occurrence_id":"01-central_pool::v141-c-R004::V::clearing.local","target_occurrence_id":"01-central_pool::v141-c-R004::V::execution.energy_trade","source_unit_id":"01-central_pool::v141-a-M01::clearing.local","target_unit_id":"01-central_pool::v141-a-M01::execution.energy_trade","omega":{"market_type":"LEM","network_level":null,"jurisdiction":null,"pricing_scope":null,"time_scale":null,"participant_types":[],"trading_stage":"activation","context_text":"Executed energy-exchange quantities in the lower-level community microgrid market-clearing problem. | Internal community energy exchanges for each entity u at time t. | Internal community imports and exports by the same entity within the same time period. | Internal energy-exchange quantities across all community entities at each modeled time period.","unknown_fields":["network_level","jurisdiction","pricing_scope","time_scale","participant_types"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-e011","v141-b-g02-E08","v141-b-g02-E11","v141-b-g02-E16","v141-b-g03-e30"]},"active":true,"source_signature":"a5e9677e4d01fed92ab7a79ebb20b578c33fead69275bd6c5cad6dfae1afb36c","relation_scope":"original_occurrence_pair_only","internal_to_parent":true,"source_science":{"mechanism_id":"v141-a-M01","source_definition":"Community member assets and internal/external exchanges are selected jointly in a common optimization problem with internal exchange conservation. Central versus distributed solution does not change this minimal allocation principle.","target_definition":"Contract performance, exchange or delivery conditions in this mechanism: Joint community dispatch of energy, reserve and peak power; entity-balance dual prices include an operator fee; upper-level non-deterioration profit sharing.","constraints":[{"constraint_id":"v141-c-R004-C001","kind":"procedural","role":"core","statement":"Local market clearing determines the executed energy-exchange quantities. Scope: Executed energy-exchange quantities in the lower-level community microgrid market-clearing problem.","expression":null,"formalization_origin":"not_formalized","template_id":null,"members":["clearing.local","execution.energy_trade"],"variable_refs":[],"parameter_refs":[],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-e011","v141-b-g02-E35"]}],"evidence":[{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g01-e011","location":{"location_id":"src-13c261d954-p04-c2r3__v141-a-M01-clearing","page":4,"printed_page":null,"section":"3.1. The bilevel model","anchor_text":"th level objective functions are different, and represent conflicting inter- n- ests. Conversely, in","equation_id":null,"figure_id":null,"table_id":null,"image_ref":"pages/page-04.png","occurrence_role":"definition"},"source_text":"Conversely, in power system economics [29-32], bilevel programming is typically used to access dual variables, which represent market prices within the marginal pricing framework [21]. This is the main reason to adopt a bilevel formulation in this paper. In the proposed bilevel model, the lower level solves the community microgrid market clearing problem, by determining: the executed quantities, the community prices, the community symmetric reserve, and the community peak power, with the aim of maximizing the social welfare of the community."},{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g02-E35","location":{"location_id":"src-13c261d954-p04-c2r3__v141-a-M01-clearing","page":4,"printed_page":null,"section":"3.1","anchor_text":"th level objective functions are different, and represent conflicting inter- n- ests. Conversely, in","equation_id":null,"figure_id":null,"table_id":null,"image_ref":"pages/page-04.png","occurrence_role":"definition"},"source_text":"In the proposed bilevel model, the lower level solves the community microgrid market clearing problem, by determining: the executed quantities, the community prices, the community symmetric reserve, and the community peak power, with the aim of maximizing the social welfare of the community. Then, the role of the upper level is to share among the entities the profits of the community, by ensuring that no entity is penalized with respect to acting individually."}],"omega":{"market_type":"LEM","network_level":null,"jurisdiction":null,"pricing_scope":null,"time_scale":null,"participant_types":[],"trading_stage":"activation","context_text":"Executed energy-exchange quantities in the lower-level community microgrid market-clearing problem. | Internal community energy exchanges for each entity u at time t. | Internal community imports and exports by the same entity within the same time period. | Internal energy-exchange quantities across all community entities at each modeled time period.","unknown_fields":["network_level","jurisdiction","pricing_scope","time_scale","participant_types"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-e011","v141-b-g02-E08","v141-b-g02-E11","v141-b-g02-E16","v141-b-g03-e30"]},"source_record":{"edge_id":"v141-c-R004-E001","source":"clearing.local","target":"execution.energy_trade","type":"links","constraint_ids":["v141-c-R004-C001"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-e011"]},"paper_scope_note":"Operational responsibilities, lower-level clearing output, energy valuation, fees, and upper-level sharing are kept separate; the price equation retains import/export and complementary slackness conditions. The ordering of the two-level LP is limited only to the unique-solution and cascaded-solution branches."}});
